package data.device.api

import kotlin.test.Test
import kotlin.test.assertEquals
import kotlin.test.assertTrue

/**
 * Three real `adb exec-out uiautomator dump /dev/tty` payloads captured from a Pixel 8
 * (`shiba`, Android 16 / API 36) on 2026-10-16, committed **verbatim** -- byte-for-byte
 * what the device wrote to stdout, including the non-XML trailer adb appends.
 *
 * Inline literals, not `src/test/resources`: no resources directory exists anywhere
 * in this repo and loading one across Android/iOS/desktop would need wiring this spec does
 * not budget for. Same convention as [PngTrimTest] and [WmOutputParserTest].
 *
 * No escaping was needed -- none of the three payloads contains `${'$'}`, a triple quote,
 * a backslash or a CR, so each raw string is byte-faithful as written. Verify that claim
 * before hand-editing anything here; the point of these fixtures is that they are NOT
 * hand-written.
 *
 * See `.pipeline/sdd/docs/measure-mode/execution/T-1/spike-note.md` for timings, density
 * and the bounds analysis.
 */

